<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:07:36 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Eisenkot says Netanyahu ‘cannot remain’ after alleged election interference by aide</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261116-eisenkot-netanyahu-cannot-stay-in-office</link><description>
Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot said on Sunday caretaker premier Benjamin Netanyahu must leave office immediately following reports of alleged electoral interference by a Netanyahu aide. The former army chief called Netanyahu and his entourage an immediate threat to democracy, hours after representatives discussed forming a national unity government.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">615a1e8c-e16f-11f1-b66f-d18c20ac47cd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:47:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg">© Ohad Zwigenberg, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Hundreds of thousands of Czechs protest in Prague over public media funding plan</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261116-czechs-protest-prague-public-media-funding-plan</link><description>
Hundreds of thousands of Czechs rallied in Prague on Sunday against government plans to replace public media fees with direct state funding, which critics say threatens broadcasters’ independence. Organisers said turnout exceeded a March protest of more than 200,000, potentially making it the largest demonstration since the 1989 Velvet Revolution.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d037ba6a-d0a0-11f1-8d05-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/10affafaee5f28571633ca44da4bc7b0878ca790.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d037ba6a-d0a0-11f1-8d05-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/10affafaee5f28571633ca44da4bc7b0878ca790.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">785cc900-e164-11f1-95d2-5fe4704a4c36</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 02:28:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d037ba6a-d0a0-11f1-8d05-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/10affafaee5f28571633ca44da4bc7b0878ca790.jpg">© Michal Cizek, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Technology</category><title>Elon Musk, Uber co-founder join calls to reinstate Jensen Huang as Nvidia chief</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20261115-elon-musk-uber-co-founder-jensen-huang-nvidia-reinstate</link><description>
Elon Musk and an Uber co-founder were among more than 158,000 signatories by Sunday demanding Jensen Huang’s reinstatement as Nvidia chief pending an independent investigation. Huang resigned Thursday after revelations of two extramarital affairs, one with a subordinate and another with a woman accused of spying for China, ending his 33-year tenure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd289ba6-e14a-11f1-b70a-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/3b627129681c154dbbef07505efac18879f6bf0c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd289ba6-e14a-11f1-b70a-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/3b627129681c154dbbef07505efac18879f6bf0c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">133b43ac-e14c-11f1-a805-53956993af7f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:31:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd289ba6-e14a-11f1-b70a-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/3b627129681c154dbbef07505efac18879f6bf0c.jpg">© Kent NISHIMURA, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Miguel Angel Felix Gallardo, architect of Mexico’s drug trade, dies age 80</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261115-miguel-angel-felix-gallardo-mexican-drug-lord-dies</link><description>
Miguel Angel Felix Gallardo, a founder of Mexico’s Guadalajara cartel known as the “boss of bosses”, died in hospital on Sunday aged 80 after suffering multiple organ failure, Jalisco state’s security ministry said. Imprisoned since 1989, he had been transferred from prison to the hospital two days before his death.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3174496-e145-11f1-ae4a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7JM9ZV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3174496-e145-11f1-ae4a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7JM9ZV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a7fa30ac-e142-11f1-a70a-f7625ce3d617</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:48:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3174496-e145-11f1-ae4a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D7JM9ZV.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sport</category><title>Kroupi on target as France beat Turkey to reach Nations League quarters</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261115-kroupi-on-target-as-france-beat-turkey-to-reach-nations-league-quarters</link><description>
Eli Junior Kroupi scored his maiden goal for France as Les Bleus beat Turkey 2-1 in Bordeaux on Sunday to top their group with 13 points and qualify for the quarter-finals of the Nations League. World Cup winners Spain, who lost at home against England, are among their potential opponents in the last eight.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09dbae92-e13c-11f1-9656-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T212617Z-1348272870-UP1EMBF1NJSWK-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-UEFANATIONS-FRA-TUR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09dbae92-e13c-11f1-9656-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T212617Z-1348272870-UP1EMBF1NJSWK-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-UEFANATIONS-FRA-TUR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">599d1588-e13c-11f1-82d2-d91e1fb91544</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:13:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/09dbae92-e13c-11f1-9656-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T212617Z-1348272870-UP1EMBF1NJSWK-RTRMADP-3-SOCCER-UEFANATIONS-FRA-TUR.jpg">© Stephane Mahe, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Nearly 2,200 migrants reach Spain's Canary Islands in two days</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-nearly-2200-migrants-reach-spain-canary-islands-in-two-days</link><description>
Nearly 2,200 migrants have reached the Canary Islands over the past two days, Spain’s coastguard said Sunday, continuing a recent surge of arrivals from West African countries to the Spanish archipelago, where the authorities declared a migration emergency earlier this week.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dfa79f7e-e112-11f1-89dc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T193226Z-188193535-RC2HMOAF3FWG-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CANARY-ISLANDS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dfa79f7e-e112-11f1-89dc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T193226Z-188193535-RC2HMOAF3FWG-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CANARY-ISLANDS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e48b4fd4-e137-11f1-98fc-31a496fd7ac9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:06:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dfa79f7e-e112-11f1-89dc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T193226Z-188193535-RC2HMOAF3FWG-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CANARY-ISLANDS.jpg">© Borja Suarez, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's Houthis advance on Aden as government forces retreat to defend their capital</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-yemen-houthis-advance-to-within-60-kilometres-of-aden-military-sources-say</link><description>
Houthi forces in Yemen have advanced to within 60 kilometres of Aden, the seat of the country's internationally recognised government, military and government sources said Sunday. The embattled government earlier announced it was pulling back its last forces from the Bab el-Mandeb Strait to defend its temporary capital on the southern coast of Yemen. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92e0513c-e12a-11f1-8ab7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T135302Z-1473180222-RC26OOADAAUR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-DETAINEES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92e0513c-e12a-11f1-8ab7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T135302Z-1473180222-RC26OOADAAUR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-DETAINEES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f89ab374-e129-11f1-810f-b5965fbe9753</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:28:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92e0513c-e12a-11f1-8ab7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T135302Z-1473180222-RC26OOADAAUR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-DETAINEES.jpg">© Khaled Abdullah, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Pragues's fight for public TV - Why Renowned Presenter Will Leave Czech TV Over Reforms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-pragues-s-fight-for-public-tv-why-renowned-presenter-will-leave-czech-tv-over-reforms</link><description>
Daniel Stach, one of the Czech Republic’s best-known television presenters, tells Gavin Lee on France 24 why he is prepared to walk away from his career rather than work under changes that he says will threaten the independence of public broadcasting. As hundreds of thousands take to the streets of Prague, Stach explains why he is joining the protests against the government’s proposed overhaul of public media funding – and what is at stake for Czech television, journalism and democracy.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ff951e8-e123-11f1-87dc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/CZECH-MEDIA-POLITICS-000-D7JB7MY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1ff951e8-e123-11f1-87dc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/CZECH-MEDIA-POLITICS-000-D7JB7MY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8d791b4-e128-11f1-9f92-5506fc354913</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:13:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Estonia to close Russian border crossings after 'sabotage' attempt at drone factory</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-estonia-to-close-russian-border-crossings-after-sabotage-attempt-at-drone-factory</link><description>
Estonia will close all its border crossing points with Russia from December 1, its ​foreign minister ‌said on Sunday, following a suspected ⁠sabotage attack on an Estonian defence company that Tallinn blamed on ‌Moscow. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13c60f24-e114-11f1-9b5e-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25285374646326.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13c60f24-e114-11f1-9b5e-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25285374646326.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">548d26ea-e115-11f1-822c-b5cf2edfde7e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:05:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/13c60f24-e114-11f1-9b5e-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25285374646326.jpg">© Hendrik Osula, AP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>How did over 2,000 migrants reach the Canaries in just 48 hours?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/how-did-over-2-000-migrants-reach-the-canaries-in-just-48-hours</link><description>
Spain says nearly 2,200 migrants have arrived by boat to the Canary Islands this weekend. The strip of the Atlantic Ocean between West Africa and the Canary Islands is one of the world's deadliest migration routes – and the journey is usually made with ill-equipped dinghies and overcrowded boats. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Madrid, Sarah Morris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dfa79f7e-e112-11f1-89dc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T193226Z-188193535-RC2HMOAF3FWG-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CANARY-ISLANDS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dfa79f7e-e112-11f1-89dc-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T193226Z-188193535-RC2HMOAF3FWG-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CANARY-ISLANDS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">10322fcc-e115-11f1-9538-e18acb043b04</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:58:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel kills senior member of Hamas's military wing in Gaza strike</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-israel-kills-senior-member-of-hamas-s-military-wing-in-gaza-strike</link><description>
The Israeli military said on Sunday its forces had killed a senior member of Hamas's military wing in Gaza. The militant group confirmed the death of Samir Abu Younis, the commander of its Rafah brigade, adding that he played a prominent role in planning the October 7, 2023 attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8bd9500-e110-11f1-96bd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T084533Z-1916440832-RC27OOA15A2T-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-HAMAS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8bd9500-e110-11f1-96bd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T084533Z-1916440832-RC27OOA15A2T-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-HAMAS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5d92877e-e112-11f1-80af-bf3cc1bef008</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:41:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8bd9500-e110-11f1-96bd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T084533Z-1916440832-RC27OOA15A2T-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-HAMAS.jpg">© Haseeb Alwazeer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title><![CDATA['Record number of women elected' to US Congress & governorships across country in midterm elections]]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-record-number-of-women-elected-to-us-congress-governorships-across-country-in-midterm-elections</link><description>
Following the 2026 US midterm elections, Gavin Lee is pleased to welcome Politico Senior National Politics Reporter Lauren Fedor. She discusses the growing number of Democratic women elected to Congress and governorships, particularly mothers of young children. “There was a realisation across the map that perhaps moms were the best messenger for this,” she explains, pointing to voters' concerns about “the cost of living, affordability, how to make ends meet.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54cc366a-e10a-11f1-a9f0-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d8402e1a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54cc366a-e10a-11f1-a9f0-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d8402e1a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e754c538-e10a-11f1-85eb-35697e667a6f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:40:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran claims drone attack on US military base in Bahrain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-claims-drone-attack-on-us-military-base-in-bahrain</link><description>
Bahrain issued two alerts of potential threats on Sunday, its first such warnings since September as blasts rocked the capital, Manama. It comes after Iran targeted an airbase in the US-allied island state, ending a long lull in strikes during the Middle East War and comes as negotiations to end the conflict remain at a stalemate, with the US maintaining its naval blockade and Iran its stranglehold over the strait of Hormuz. Story by Rachael Griffiths.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc1d38c8-e108-11f1-8b7b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-160212-160405-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc1d38c8-e108-11f1-8b7b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-160212-160405-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e170475c-e108-11f1-ab96-f165ee9aaa0a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:29:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Canaries urge government action after 2,200 migrants reach the islands in 48h</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261115-canaries-urge-government-action-after-2-200-migrants-reach-the-islands-in-48h-1</link><description>
Spain says nearly 2,200 migrants have arrived by boat to the Canary Islands this weekend. The Spanish islands are one of the main entry points into Europe for migrants from Africa. The Spanish Interior Ministry says more than 13,000 arrived there between January and the end of last month. Details and analysis by Andrew Hilliar, FRANCE 24 international affairs editor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6524e48c-e108-11f1-a387-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-160718-161132-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6524e48c-e108-11f1-a387-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-160718-161132-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a1a4c02-e108-11f1-ad35-f165ee9aaa0a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:24:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Jensen Huang: The French Connection</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261115-jensen-huang-the-french-connection</link><description>
President Trump is heading to Asia in a few days time, and will meet President Putin and President Xi. There's likely to be one fewer tech giants at the table, Jensen Huang, newly resigned from Nvidia, over the suspected spy affair. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb9bfd36-e05e-11f1-85e3-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/Jensen-Huang-000-36PC88T.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cb9bfd36-e05e-11f1-85e3-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/Jensen-Huang-000-36PC88T.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fad9359a-e05f-11f1-8600-8534dcd91768</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:03:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Santa school in full swing in London ahead of Christmas celebrations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/santa-school-in-full-swing-in-london-ahead-of-christmas-celebrations</link><description>
It may still be November but it's beginning to look a lot like Christmas in South London, as many Santa impersonators are heading to school for their festive training. The school, organised by an event company called Ministry of Fun, brings together Santas, elves, and Mrs Clauses to share experiences, practice belly laughs and learn how to bring the magic of Christmas to life. Story by Rachael Griffiths.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9d5d0c4-e100-11f1-b165-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-082508-082646-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c9d5d0c4-e100-11f1-b165-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-082508-082646-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cea94b12-e100-11f1-8159-af3882b07dd6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:35:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>A deep dive into Ivory Coast's solar energy goals</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/a-deep-dive-into-ivory-coast-s-solar-energy-goals</link><description>
Can Ivory Coast, which remains heavily dependent on fossil fuels, turn to solar power to make its energy consumption greener and more sustainable? We visited the country's new solar power plant in Ferkessédougou, in the north of the country. Inaugurated in July, it is expected to generate nearly 90 gigawatt-hours of electricity a year. Report by Julia Guggenheim.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a07102cc-e0ff-11f1-86c8-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-081217-081424-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a07102cc-e0ff-11f1-86c8-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-081217-081424-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a5fb1a84-e0ff-11f1-a55d-efe590fb5315</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:25:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tech 24</category><title>Why the Nvidia scandal is bad news for Europe’s AI ambitions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261115-why-the-nvidia-scandal-is-bad-news-for-europe-s-ai-ambitions</link><description>
Nvidia's Jensen Huang poured money into open-source AI, from French-founded Hugging Face to chips for Mistral's data centres, and fought Washington's attempts to restrict it. With Huang gone and China hawks emboldened, Tech 24 asks whether Europe's AI ambitions have lost their most powerful ally, and whether he was ever the champion Europe needed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4a8bc10-e0fc-11f1-92b7-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T112739Z-857398562-RC2138AW8TLP-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-CEO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4a8bc10-e0fc-11f1-92b7-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T112739Z-857398562-RC2138AW8TLP-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-CEO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">24008492-e0ff-11f1-9fcd-efe590fb5315</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:16:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Peter O'BRIEN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US probes nationwide flights stoppage as travel disruptions persist</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-probes-nationwide-flights-stoppage-as-travel-disruptions-persist</link><description>
US air travel is expected to return to normal this Sunday, following a nationwide ground stop Friday night that stranded hundreds of thousands of passengers and disrupted travel worldwide. The Trump administration blamed the incident on a botched replacement of old copper wire communication lines and said there was no evidence this was a cyberattack. The ground stop now raises questions about the country's aging infrastructure and lawmakers are calling for an investigation. Analysis by Philip Mann, aviation expert at Vector Strategic Consulting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f68e5f6c-e0fd-11f1-91ae-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T154335Z-516903887-RC2ONOAT735S-RTRMADP-3-USA-FAA-GROUND-STOP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f68e5f6c-e0fd-11f1-91ae-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-14T154335Z-516903887-RC2ONOAT735S-RTRMADP-3-USA-FAA-GROUND-STOP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4dfc6f98-e0fc-11f1-bdc8-ebeb331f4797</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:09:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Chinese spy, chip sales, Trump ties... The Nvidia scandal deepens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/chinese-spy-chip-sales-trump-ties-the-nvidia-scandal-deepens</link><description>
The Nvidia scandal continues to unravel. Sunday, the Singapore-based company Megaspeed said that Chinese businesswoman Alice Huang had officially left the company in 2025. She is the alleged Chinese spy that had an affair with Nvidia's former CEO Jensen Huang. Late last year, revelations showed she was being investigated for chip smuggling. The scandal has also raised questions about how much the US government knew – Trump was allegedly warned about the affair but did not react. Analysis by Laïla Mörch, CEO of Shael and tech investor in Paris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4a8bc10-e0fc-11f1-92b7-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T112739Z-857398562-RC2138AW8TLP-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-CEO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b4a8bc10-e0fc-11f1-92b7-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T112739Z-857398562-RC2138AW8TLP-RTRMADP-3-NVIDIA-CEO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41ca757c-e0fb-11f1-85db-25e9b093d137</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:00:56 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>The week in pictures: Spain protests, Pope Leo's Peru 'homecoming' and Rocky fans in Philly</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261115-the-week-in-pictures-spain-protests-pope-leo-peru-homecoming-rocky-fans-philly-rosalia</link><description>
FRANCE 24 looks back at some of the week's most striking images, from angry protests over a housing crisis that has dominated Spain's election campaign, to Leo XIV's visit to his adopted homeland Peru and "Rocky" fans marking 50 years since the release of boxing movie classic.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c94a7240-e01f-11f1-b658-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317808141916.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c94a7240-e01f-11f1-b658-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317808141916.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0bb2340c-e04c-11f1-87ef-f38af753107f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:59:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c94a7240-e01f-11f1-b658-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26317808141916.jpg">© Matt Slocum, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French Ciryl Gane retains MMA heavyweaight title agianst Josh Hokit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-cyril-gane-retains-mma-heavyweaight-title-agianst-josh-hokit</link><description>
Ciryl Gane remains the world's MMA heavyweight champion. Overnight, the French athlete beat Josh Hokit in the main event of UFC 334 at Madison Square Garden in ​New York. The 5-round fight was rough, as Shirli Sitbon explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7326ff90-e0fc-11f1-99a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T052339Z-1246486452-MT1USATODAY30357052-RTRMADP-3-MMA-UFC-334.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7326ff90-e0fc-11f1-99a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T052339Z-1246486452-MT1USATODAY30357052-RTRMADP-3-MMA-UFC-334.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9314b56e-e0fb-11f1-8a2b-7b68a0c67305</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:58:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bahrain says air defences destroyed several Iranian drones attacking US base</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bahrain-says-air-defences-destroyed-several-iranian-drones-attacking-us-base</link><description>
Bahrain issued two alerts of potential threats on Sunday, its first such warnings since September. The second Iranian drone attack in three days, ending a long lull in strikes during the Middle East war. Diplomatic efforts to end the almost nine-month conflict have yet to produce a breakthrough, with ​sporadic attacks continuing. Details from the ground by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Tehran, Reza Sayah.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84b2607c-e0f9-11f1-b274-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-130317-130744-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84b2607c-e0f9-11f1-b274-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-130317-130744-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89cee620-e0f9-11f1-b619-d9dce5f4b66f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:55:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A week in France</category><title>France's presidential race heats up</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-week-in-france/20261115-france-s-presidential-race-heats-up</link><description>
In approximately six months' time, French voters will head to the polls for the first round of the presidential election. Due to term limits, current president Emmanuel Macron is barred from running again. But that hasn't stopped a whole host of candidates from tossing their hat in the ring. 
